==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk|en}}. Various unlikely theories derive it from:
* "fucked up, got ambushed, zipped in [a body bag]" (if this is not simply a [[backronym]])

Derivation from an Italian word {{m|it||*fugazi|fake}} is suggested, there are several similar word that exists in Italian, although {{compound|it|fu|cazzo|nocat=1}} ("it was shit") has been suggested as a possible primary source of derivation.

* {{cog|fr|fougasse||land mine}}; {{w|Flame fougasse|flame fougasses}} were used extensively in the Korean and Vietnam wars
* English {{m|en|fugacious}}
* Fugazy Continental Limousine, a company from New York City, once successful but later imploded amidst fraud allegations; its name entering local slang as a term for anything scammy or fraudulent.

Derivation from an Italian word {{m|it||*fugazi|fake}} is sometimes suggested, there are several word that exists in Italian, although {{compound|it|fu|cazzo|nocat=1}} ("it was shit") has been suggested as a possible primary source of derivation.

===Pronunciation===
